    basic: "In a Standard game, focus on 'killing' the opponent's Aces and Tens. Use your trumps to seize the lead when you are void in a suit, then lead your own Ten to force them to play their King or Queen into your pile.",
    intermediate: "The Seven Management: If you bid 'Seven', you must keep the 7 of Trumps until the very last turn. This means you need enough other trumps to defend yourself throughout the round so you aren't forced to play the 7 early.",
    advanced: 'Defensive Coordination: In the 2-vs-1 setup, the defenders must work together. If your partner is leading a suit, and you have the Ten, play it! You are giving points to the partnership rather than letting the declarer take them later.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Count the trumps. There are 8 in total. If you have 5 and your opponents play 2, only one remains. You are now the master of the table.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "In 'Betl', discard your highest cards (Ace, Ten) as soon as possible into suits where you are void.",
      },
